From 04c589b844faa4bfabd043f86c99fd6ecd641cc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: REG-Linux <reglinux@reglinux.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Feb 2026 00:29:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Remove SDL3 dependency: vendor one-fpga with hardcoded SDL3
 constants

Replace the one-fpga crate SDL3 dependency with a local version that
uses hardcoded SDL3 ABI-stable integer constants for Button (0-20),
Axis, and Scancode types. This eliminates the sdl3-sys bundled cmake
build that fails during cross-compilation with:
  arm-buildroot-linux-musleabihf-gcc: ERROR: unsafe header/library
  path used in cross-compilation: '-L' '/usr/local/lib'

The patched one-fpga maintains full API compatibility with mister-fpga.
